rota lap 4627, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; cut and stop. Read the fire threshold, standfast and the three depths of removal. Standfast's own line -- a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom -- named this lap's shape: the absence loom was built at one site and never carried to the second.
think Cold roster opened 251 green, 2 red. shim_reason read late_say_rostered=1 and standing_equipment read red_self BECAUSE of it, so one repair closed two reds.
think The late say was in a peer's fresh gitlink_dependent_witness: say scan.out stood at line 88 under the first assert on scan at 64, so a refusal printed the witness's own sentence and never the census that line exists to publish. Lifted above the assert; both witnesses GREEN.
think Keystone is my own named-unbuilt item from 20260911.034352 -- reds_pin_capacity_scan.sh answers pin_headroom, pin_foldable_rows and pin_deadlocked from this clone's bytes about a page eight ships write, and its header called that purely local.
think Measured before building: all 200 of the last 200 commits touched construction/REDS.md, 50 of them inside 16 hours, and headroom moved 0 -> 1993 -> 15 bytes across five of them -- a swing wider than the median row of 1977. So a clone one commit behind reads a ledger whose deadlock verdict can have flipped.
think Wired the reading the way the sibling reds_spine_derive_scan.sh does: read the anointed REF rather than fetching, since the round-open pulls at lap start and eight ships fetching every lap buys nothing. A ref that will not resolve reads unread rather than falling back to local.
think Added mode=all_rows to reds_pin_capacity_rows.awk so both pins are read by the ONE row reader; a second spelling of what a row is would be the drift that file exists to prevent.
obs The reading fired on its own lap, on live state: mid-lap commits_behind went 0 -> 2 and it named %705, the very row this checkout's pin_foldable_rows=1 was counting, already folded by a peer. Replayed eight commits back on real history it names %701 -- the row that misled the lap of 034352.
obs My first wording said a peer has folded it, which is an inference the bytes cannot support: my own unpushed row reads identically. %700's own sentence, an hour old, turned on my line. Renamed to pin_row_ahead_of_upstream, naming the observation and both readings of it.
obs Reported, never gated, for the reason dropped_upstream_stamps is reported one guard over: being behind is ordinary work on an eight-ship fleet, and a gate that reds on ordinary work is a gate somebody turns off.
obs The witness pinned the pen's leg COUNT beside cases_failed=0 -- a deleted leg read exactly like a leg that never failed, so 28 new legs could have been lifted one at a time under a green witness.
obs A reach leg over the tree's own run bit where the pen stayed green, which is the predicate-versus-reach split the one_clock_mono repair taught this room two laps ago.
loom witness=reds_pin_capacity control_legs=83 control_fails=0 mutations_bitten=5
loom scan=reds_pin_capacity pin_bytes=40944 pin_bound=40960 pin_headroom=16 commits_behind=0
loom roster=cold guards_run=255 green=251 red=2 gated=2 seconds=2764
obs The hot pass found three more reds and all three were instructive. The ledger headline read 687 against its own derived 688, since a row added is a row the headline must count. My own new row was cited by NUMBER on the card before xy had bound it, which rule 4 of the derived spine forbids and unshared_citation caught; it is cited by stamp now. And unsaid_rostered read 938 against a ceiling of 936 -- measured with my changes stashed it read 938 too, so the two are a PEER's, arriving on my rebase.
obs Those two are the new mantra_annotate_cli_witness's seat and bounded bindings, asserted on and holding nothing to say because they run grep -q. Given grep -n they have a capture worth reporting on both paths -- a refusal shows which half of the seat went missing, a green run names where in main.rye it stands. Captain's repair in a peer's lane; their witness GREEN after it.
obs And last lap's own card_pin_claim caught THIS card: my YOURS line claimed the pin was walled with nothing foldable while the instrument read pin_foldable_rows=1, my own BOOKED row being foldable. The card cites the scan now rather than spelling a number. A guard written one lap ago refusing its author's next card is the loom working exactly as built.
obs My own witness broke the rule I had just repaired in a peer's: three asserts on a live binding that never said its capture. Fixed in the same breath.
obs The send's rebase met three conflicts and every one was a peer working the same ground. A peer had made the SAME gitlink_dependent repair independently, in better words, citing the same guard -- I took theirs. And the pre-push spine caught %708 double-booked: xy published its own at 20260911.055500 against my 20260911.064500, so the earlier stamp keeps the number and my row renumbered to %709. That is rule 4 of the derived spine paying for itself -- the card and the log cited by STAMP, so the renumber touched the ledger alone and swept nothing.
